From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Enrico=20B=C3=BChler?= <enrico.buehler@unom.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] pipewire: give a streaming host a private capture node

Steam's Game Recording links to the node the gamescope_pipewire protocol
announces as soon as a game starts, and sets the stream's focus appid to
that game. The node is reliable since pfhdr18, and PipeWire 1.6 hands a
reliable frame to one link only. Steam took every frame, and a streaming
host on the same node froze while its audio played on.

Publish a second node, gamescope-capture, that no protocol names. It is
reliable and paints the whole session at focus appid 0 on its own. The
announced node keeps upstream's recycling and its name, so Steam and any
other reader share it as before. Each streaming node composites once per
vblank.

Stamp pfhdr34.
